  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_2",
  "label": "User projected onto the visual material as the moral authority figure",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material (the Black man) as the moral authority figure ('my brother') who is delivering the advice. The text explicitly identifies the man as 'my brother', which creates an analogical mapping where the user is implicitly positioned as the 'sibling' or 'relative' who is being addressed by this moral figure. This projection reinforces the stereotype that Black men are inherently moral authorities or figures of wisdom, which is part of the racialized moralistic trope.",
